/documentation\/shortestpaths","title":"ShortestPaths","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/DijkstraSearch":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DijkstraSearch"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/dijkstrasearch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm as a sequence of "},{"code":"DijkstraSearchEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, pulled one at a time. It holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy of the graph and the weight closure, so later changes to the original do not affect it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and it can be iterated more than once. Vertices are numbered once, and the search keeps its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distances in arrays over that numbering."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearch","type":"topic","title":"DijkstraSearch","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DijkstraSearch"}]}}}